The module compiles cleanly. It uses an asynchronous active-high reset by including `posedge areset` in the sensitivity list, and clears `q` to zero whenever `areset` is asserted; otherwise it captures `d` on the rising edge of `clk`.

```verilog
module TopModule (
    input        clk,
    input        areset,
    input  [7:0] d,
    output reg [7:0] q
);

    always @(posedge clk or posedge areset) begin
        if (areset)
            q <= 8'b0;
        else
            q <= d;
    end

endmodule
```
